What a column's mean loses: variance of depth among points less variance of the column means (mean over windows), by height: 0.67 at 127996; 0.45 at 63998; 0.23 at 31999; 0.33 at 16000; 0.42 at 8000; 0.38 at 4000; 0.42 at 2000; 0.32 at 1000
The equation gives 0.52 D = 0.56 for the mean over the slab's thickness alone (D / (2 sqrt(pi nu)) x (8/15) sqrt(4)); the mean across the column's width takes off more, and the few points of a column add some back.

